window.GUIDE_INDEX = {"locale":"de","words":{"ph":"Handbuch durchsuchen","no":"Nichts gefunden","n":"{n} Treffer","n1":"1 Treffer","hint":"Zum Suchen / drücken"},"sections":[{"p":"accounts.html","a":"","t":"Sicherheit & Problembehebung","u":"","b":"Sicherheit & Problembehebung What your passphrase protects, what Daimond asks before it acts, what stays private, and what to do when something is wrong."},{"p":"accounts.html","a":"s1","t":"Ihr Konto ist eine Passphrase","u":"Sicherheit & Problembehebung","b":"On first run Daimond generates a passphrase of eight random words and shows it once. It is the key to everything stored here. It is not sent anywhere, it is not stored in the clear, and nobody can reset it. It unlocks everything encrypted here, meaning your provider keys, your mail credentials and the account's own signing key, and the key that seals the sync parcel is derived from it too. The signing key is what signs you in for credits. Forget the passphrase and the encrypted data is gone. Once a passphrase is in place you can add a Passkey for a faster unlock, by face, fingerprint or security key. It unseals the passphrase for you instead of replacing it, so the passphrase stays the fallback. The unlock happens on the device, and the credits service only ever sees a public key."},{"p":"accounts.html","a":"s2","t":"Die Bedienelemente für das Konto","u":"Sicherheit & Problembehebung","b":"Your name is at the top of the account area, at the foot of the rail. Change name&hellip; und Change passphrase&hellip; do what they say, and the second re-wraps your encrypted data under the new passphrase. Add a passkey&hellip; Backup exportieren writes your chats, diamonds, workspace files and your account key to a file you keep. Import a backup&hellip; adopts the backup's account where this browser holds none, and where one is already here it brings back only the work. Abmelden locks the app. Your data stays on the device, encrypted. Forget this identity&hellip; removes the account and its encrypted data from this browser for good. Beside them, Synchronisierung turns this device's sync on or off, and Diagnose shows and copies the app's own log, which holds event names and a clock, with no keys, no message text and nothing from your files. That log is what to paste into a report."},{"p":"accounts.html","a":"s3","t":"Moving your account","u":"Sicherheit & Problembehebung","b":"Your account is a signing key held in this browser. The passphrase does not recreate it , and only decrypts the copy stored here. So the same passphrase in a fresh browser starts a separate account, with its own credits and no Pro. The key itself has to travel, and three things carry it. Weiteres Gerät verknüpfen , which shows a pairing code. A passkey, which stands a new device up in one gesture. Backup exportieren , whose file holds the key for Import a backup&hellip; to adopt in a browser that has none. Do one of them before you retire a browser. Once its storage is gone, with no backup taken and no other device linked, the key is gone with it. A backup holds your work in the clear and your key wrapped under your passphrase. Importing the file alone makes nobody you. Whoever holds the file und the passphrase holds the account, which is why the two should not travel together."},{"p":"accounts.html","a":"s4","t":"Mehr als eine Person an einem Browser","u":"Sicherheit & Problembehebung","b":"One browser can hold several accounts, each with its own chats, keys, credits and files. ＋ Weiteres Konto hinzufügen makes a second, and the row above it switches between them. Switching locks the first and forgets its keys before opening the other. Nobody sees another account's data."},{"p":"accounts.html","a":"s5","t":"What Daimond asks before it acts","u":"Sicherheit & Problembehebung","b":"A chip beside the model says what Daimond does without asking. It has three settings, and they apply to the whole app. Ask every time reads Every command is put to you first. So is reaching the web, once in each conversation. Guarded reads Commands run. Once something written by somebody else has been read, Daimond asks before reaching out. It is the default. Bypass reads Nothing is asked, whatever has been read. Under Guarded, once a turn has read something written by somebody else, such as a web page, an email or a build log, anything it then wants to fetch or send is put to you first, and a command in that turn runs with the network refused. That is the case where text you did not write could talk Daimond into carrying your work somewhere. Switching to Bypass asks once, and says what you give up. No mode moves the fence a command runs inside, a diamond's folders, the system-call filter, or the log you can read afterwards. An agent working on its own is asked about separately. Clicking something on a page can spend money or submit a form, and none of that can be taken back, so a click by an unattended agent is put to you even under looser settings. Money has its own brakes, and t"},{"p":"accounts.html","a":"s6","t":"Was privat bleibt","u":"Sicherheit & Problembehebung","b":"Your passphrase, provider keys, mail credentials, chats, diamonds and files live in this browser and are not sent to us. What we hold is money and ciphertext, meaning your balance and licences and, for sync, a parcel we cannot open. Your messages reach a model provider directly with your own key, or through our metered service when you spend credits. Fetching a page, and syncing or sending mail, pass through the gateway. So the honest claim is that with your own key nothing of your work reaches us in the clear, and that you can watch only ciphertext leave for our servers. You need not take that on trust. The code running in this browser is public, it builds byte for byte from that source, and every build served is sealed into a published record. Verify this build , in the About dialog, checks the one you are running. Open your browser's network panel and watch where the calls go. The protection has limits. A passphrase guards against someone opening the browser's developer tools, and not against a compromised browser, a malicious extension or a keylogger, which defeat any in-browser scheme. And what a remote server does inside itself cannot be proven from outside, which is why it i"},{"p":"accounts.html","a":"s7","t":"When something goes wrong","u":"Sicherheit & Problembehebung","b":"Connect a model to start. No model is connected. Add one, or add a key for the provider already listed. Your second device is empty. You made a second account instead of pairing. Pair it, or import a backup. See Mehr als ein Gerät . A shared folder is not arriving. It is over the 200 MiB a shared folder may weigh. A banner names it. Share a smaller folder. Not valid JSON. Nothing saved. A hand edit to a diamond's memory left the file unreadable, so nothing was written. Fix the text or close without saving. Nothing runs on its own. The light is red because the action is stopped. Press play on the light beside it. Terminal needs the Daimond Hand on this computer. Install&hellip; beside it goes to Dein Rechner . A turn is sitting on another device. That machine is probably waiting for a folder permission on its own screen. Go and look, or press Run here . A panel has disappeared. It is unpinned, and still there. The ⋯ chip opens the gallery, and Ctrl K reaches any panel by name. Everything is locked after a reload. The key is held in memory and nowhere else, unless this device is set to stay unlocked across reloads. Enter the passphrase, or use a passkey. Still stuck? The rail holds a"},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"","t":"Chats & Diamonds","u":"","b":"Chats & Diamonds A chat is a conversation. A diamond is a saved project with its own memory, its own page and its own files. You keep the one inside the other."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s1","t":"A chat","u":"Chats & Diamonds","b":"Die + neben Chats starts one. Type in the box and send. A new chat is titled Neuer Chat until you say something, and after that its first line is its title. While an answer is arriving you can keep typing. A message sent then waits as a dashed bubble and goes as its own turn when the answer finishes. Click it to take it back, or its cross to drop it. Pressing stop hands anything queued back to you, unsent. Deleting a chat moves it to the Trash, so nothing asks first. The two acts that cannot be undone are the ones that ask, and both are in that panel."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s2","t":"Reading a long thread","u":"Chats & Diamonds","b":"Each turn is a labelled tile, so you can see at a glance who said what. Every turn is a tile, labelled You , Thinking , Tool , Daimond , or as a note from the app itself. Each header carries the local date and time to the minute in the Holocene reckoning, so 12026-09-15 13:12 is this year plus ten thousand. Hover for the full instant with its offset. The header of the chat carries the controls. Show steps shows the work done between your message and the answer. Collapse answers leaves only what you asked. It is the quickest way to skim, and how you start picking turns. Short answers is a standing request for brevity in this chat. It is a file in your workspace that you can edit, not a hidden instruction. The permission chip reads Guarded , Ask every time or Bypass . See Sicherheit & Problembehebung . Two chevrons beside the send button walk back through your own messages and return to the end."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s3","t":"What a stop looks like","u":"Chats & Diamonds","b":"A turn says how it ended, in exact words. Answered means it finished and said something. Stopped means you pressed stop. Step limit reached means it ran out of rounds. Ended without saying anything means the model returned nothing at all. Ended without an answer, after reasoning means it thought, was asked once to answer or use a tool, and still said nothing. Ended on an error , oder Ended: the tool call arrived as text , say what they say. None of these is dressed up as an answer."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s4","t":"Keeping a chat","u":"Chats & Diamonds","b":"Two buttons sit on a chat's row in the rail. Keep turns the whole conversation into a diamond. Fold all turns it into a diamond by summarising it, keeping what was worked out and dropping the back-and-forth. To keep only part, collapse the answers, tick the turns worth keeping, and choose Ausgewählte einklappen . Fold a step you have adopted, and leave a passing remark where it is. Nothing is absorbed on its own. A diamond's memory changes only through a fold or an edit, and every write is kept in History."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s5","t":"Inside a diamond","u":"Chats & Diamonds","b":"Your diamonds sit above your chats, and the + makes one. A diamond has two faces, and a switch in its header moves between them. Kristall is what it knows, and Chat is its own conversation. What this diamond knows , on the Crystal face. The raw file is one press away. The card lists the diamond's title and summary in its own words, then everything else it holds, a line each. Edit opens a form. Show raw memory opens the file itself, for when you would rather work in it directly."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s6","t":"The four files a diamond keeps","u":"Chats & Diamonds","b":"Memory is kept in the open. Four files sit in the diamond's own folder, readable in the Workspace panel and by the daimon. crystal.json holds what this diamond is , meaning its title, summary, sections, facts and links. REQUIREMENTS.md holds what is to do, as objectives with ranked tasks under each. A task leaves it by being ticked or struck out, and by nothing else. DECISIONS.md holds what was ruled, dated, with the reason. New rulings are appended, and old ones are left as they were. STATE.md holds where things are now, and is overwritten each time. All four ride with the daimon on every round inside one budget, so what a diamond is told about itself is bounded and predictable. A crystal too large to fit whole keeps its overflow readable and searchable instead of dropping it. The counts on the card, Objectives , Open tasks und Done , are read off REQUIREMENTS.md ."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s7","t":"Two kinds of fold","u":"Chats & Diamonds","b":"The word covers two different acts. Summarise earlier messages , in the chat header, is the app compressing a conversation that no longer fits. Its decisions are filed into DECISIONS.md , its open items into REQUIREMENTS.md , and its next step into STATE.md . What it files can be found afterwards, and what it leaves in a notice cannot. Fold now , on the Crystal face, is a model rewriting what this diamond remembers from what has happened since. Every write snapshots a version. Filing is repeatable, so running the same fold twice files nothing twice, and the order two folds arrive in does not change what the files end up saying."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s8","t":"History","u":"Chats & Diamonds","b":"History lists every version, newest first. Ansehen reads one, Wiederherstellen makes it current again, and Delta shows the material a fold was given. Restore keeps what was current first, so a restore can itself be undone."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s9","t":"Acting without being asked","u":"Chats & Diamonds","b":"A diamond answers when you prompt it and at no other time, unless you set up a triggered action. Those live under When this diamond acts on the Crystal face, and Add an action makes one. Two things can set one off, either minutes of your own activity, counted only while you work, or mail arriving in a folder you name. Each action carries an instruction, sent every time, and a context, sent once until you change it. They are an ordinary file, triggers.json , in the diamond's folder. A new action is stopped , and says so: Stopped. Press &#9654; on the light beside the pulldown to let this action run. One press arms it."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s10","t":"The light","u":"Chats & Diamonds › Acting without being asked","b":"Every action, every diamond and the Alles row wear the same three-part control, a play, a pause and a round light. The light says whether anything is armed and free to fire. Red. Nothing here will act by itself. Amber. Some of it will, and some is held. Green. Everything set up will act. A fresh account is red everywhere, which is the honest answer to whether anything is running by itself. An action missing its mailbox or its instruction is left out of the count, because it could not fire. Amber can only be arrived at, never set. A held action spends nothing, because it is refused before the turn starts."},{"p":"chats-and-diamonds.html","a":"s11","t":"Tags, links and the Trash","u":"Chats & Diamonds","b":"Tags on the Crystal face files a diamond in the rail. Up to eight tags, lowercased and deduplicated. Suggested offers four to start from. Tags are inert. They are not sent to a model, they are no part of the memory, and they change nothing an agent does. Nach Tag filtern in the rail narrows by them. A diamond can also be linked to another, and the Graph is the picture of that. Deleting a chat or a diamond trashes it. It is still stored and still synced, out of every daimon's reach, and kept thirty days with the date on the row. Wiederherstellen brings it back on every device. Endgültig löschen und Papierkorb leeren are the two that ask. &larr; The interface Next: A diamond&rsquo;s page &rarr;"},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"","t":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web","u":"","b":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web A daimon works from files it can read and write, folders you hand it, mail you can answer, and pages it can show or drive."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s1","t":"Der Arbeitsbereich","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web","b":"Die Schaltfläche Workspace panel shows your files as an ordinary tree. Three chips at the top name where the workspace lives. Browser is this browser's own private storage, reachable by nothing outside Daimond. It is the default, and it syncs to your other devices. Rechner is a real folder on this computer's disk. Daimond works in it directly, so the same files are in your file manager. It stays on that computer, and travels only if you share it with the ⇄ control. Chromium-based browsers only. Cloud is where the bytes are kept, which is what lets a workspace be larger than the device holding it. It is not a third place to work. Files are encrypted before they leave. The folder you open as Rechner is the whole of what Daimond can see, with nothing above it and nothing beside it."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s2","t":"Getting a file in","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web › Der Arbeitsbereich","b":"Dateien hochladen , the arrow-into-tray in the header, takes one file or a handful. Import a folder&hellip; copies a folder in, after which it syncs like everything else. Einen echten Ordner öffnen with the Rechner chip. Nothing is copied, and it syncs only if you share it. Mail arrives here as ordinary files, and a daimon writes here where it is allowed to."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s3","t":"Held, in the cloud, or pinned","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web › Der Arbeitsbereich","b":"A file is in one of three states, and the tree says which. Held means it is on this device. In cloud storage means it is only there, marked with a cloud, and clicking it brings it down. Angeheftet means it is never freed automatically. As storage fills, the files longest unused go back to the cloud on their own. Freeing is not deleting, since the file is still listed and comes back when asked for. A daimon is told plainly when a file it wants is in the cloud, and has to fetch it deliberately. A cap limits how much it may bring down on its own."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s4","t":"Handing a folder over","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web","b":"The paperclip on every row reads Attach to current focus . What it does follows what is in focus, whichever row it sits on. A diamond is in focus. The file or folder joins that diamond's workspace and stays until you take it out. A chat is in focus. The attachment is for the next turn only. Attaching copies nothing. The file stays where it is and the diamond points at it, so attaching one folder to two diamonds still leaves one folder. Each attachment is either Note , meaning the path is worth knowing and costs a few tokens, or Read , meaning the contents are wanted now. Start with Note, which is much the cheaper. Either way the text it generates goes into the message box in front of what you type, where you can edit or delete it. Ticking a folder in the workspace group is the permission, so this chat or diamond may then read and change what is inside. Ticking a file only puts it in front of the model. A diamond's Reach row names every folder it may write in, and says so in both trees."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s5","t":"What a daimon can open","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web › Handing a folder over","b":"A daimon can open only what is in its diamond's workspace. Nothing else is readable or writable through the file tools, by the daimon or by any helper it dispatches. The check is in compiled code at the one door every file tool passes, and that code is in a bundle that builds reproducibly from public source, so it is not an instruction in a prompt. That rule settles what a daimon can reach and says nothing about where what it reads ends up, because whatever it opens goes to your model provider with the rest of the turn."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s6","t":"The attachment list","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web › Handing a folder over","b":"Rows carry an age, Added {when} . A path that is no longer there is drawn as Gone with no open action, so a dead row never poses as a live one. Anything a daimon attached for itself, such as a fold's harvest or a file an agent kept, sits under one collapsed heading, Added by the daimon , with a count and a Drop all . Your own attachments stay where they are."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s7","t":"Sharing a folder to your other devices","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web › Handing a folder over","b":"A Rechner folder lives on one computer, and your phone cannot open it. The ⇄ control on the row is how it reaches one anyway, with Share with devices that lack native access . Off, only devices that can open the folder themselves see it. On, it is copied to your other devices, up to 200 MiB per folder. The setting is per folder, whichever device you set it from, and only a device that can open the folder can set it. A folder over the ceiling is left out whole, and a banner says which one and what it weighed. Share a smaller folder, or take some of it out."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s8","t":"Documents, and books","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web","b":"Open a .typ file and the Doc panel gains two buttons. Compile lays the document out in the page and writes a preview PDF beside the source, and while those pages are up, every save rebuilds them. Press it on a chapter and it compiles the document that includes the chapter, then takes you to that chapter's page. Both panels have to be on screen for the loop to run. Where the window is too narrow, the Doc panel says so, and one rebuild catches up when they return. The editor need not be Daimond's. A save from any editor writing into the granted folder is picked up within about a second. A phone cannot hold a book's files or afford the memory a layout costs, so it hands the compile to a paired computer that can, sealed to your account exactly as a turn is, and the laid-out pages come back."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s9","t":"Jede Art von Datei","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web","b":"Any file is stored and travels, up to a gigabyte each. A document or a spreadsheet opens as a reading view , which shows what it says and not how it prints. Values are as stored, formulas are not recalculated, and macros are neither run nor read. Save a copy writes one to your own device and leaves the file here untouched. Where nothing recognises a file, its bytes are shown, and the panel says so."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s10","t":"E-Mail","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web","b":"A browser cannot open a mail connection, so Daimond connects through the gateway, which hands back the raw message and forgets your credential. Your mail is written into the workspace as ordinary files. Add a mailbox with the + in the Email panel. Type your address and Daimond guesses the server settings, and every field stays editable. Most providers want an app password in place of your account password, and the panel says where to find it. The credential is stored on this device under your passphrase, handed to the gateway for one sync, and forgotten. Daimond stores no mail on any server. Only you can send. A daimon can draft a message into the Compose panel. The Send button is the one thing that puts mail on the wire, and only a person can press it. Email is part of Daimond Pro."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s11","t":"Das Web-Panel","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web","b":"Ask Daimond to open a page, or paste a link. There are three ways, and the site decides which works. Show it. The page appears in the panel. Most sites refuse to be embedded, so this works for a minority. Read it. Daimond fetches the page and reads its text. It works where showing does not. You do not see the page, and Daimond does. Drive it. With the browser add-on, Daimond opens a real tab, signed in as you, and works it while you watch. It is the only way to work a live, logged-in site. Signing in stays yours. When you sign in on a driven page, Daimond stops watching entirely, taking no text, no picture and no keystrokes, and never sees your password. You hand the wheel back from the browser tab and not from Daimond, so a page cannot take it from you."},{"p":"email-web-files.html","a":"s12","t":"Werkzeuge","u":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web","b":"Die Schaltfläche Werkzeuge panel says what Daimond can do. Built-in tools are already yours and free, and the panel lists exactly what is held, so it cannot promise one that is not there. Packs are extras, bought once, in dollars. &larr; A diamond&rsquo;s page Next: Your computer &rarr;"},{"p":"index.html","a":"","t":"Hier anfangen","u":"","b":"Hier anfangen Daimond is an AI workspace that runs in your browser, and your chats, keys and files stay on this device. You connect a model, talk to it, and keep what works. No server holds your account. Whatever leaves the browser is named on the page of this guide that covers it. The main ones are a message to the model provider you connected, a page fetched for you, a mailbox synced, and an encrypted parcel sent to a device you linked. First run. The centre lists three steps, and the one you are at is drawn as the button."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s1","t":"Three steps to a first answer","u":"Hier anfangen","b":""},{"p":"index.html","a":"s2","t":"Make your account","u":"Hier anfangen › Three steps to a first answer","b":"Type a name, and Daimond generates a passphrase of eight random words and shows it once. Write it down. It unlocks everything stored here, and nobody can reset it. Then choose Konto anlegen . A password manager is a fine place for it, since eight random words are hard to guess. Under the button, Have a passcode or a pairing code? opens two other routes, redeeming a passcode for an account with credits and pairing this browser to a device you already use. If you already have Daimond elsewhere, pair instead of creating, or you will end up with two accounts."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s3","t":"Connect a model","u":"Hier anfangen › Three steps to a first answer","b":"A daimon thinks with a model, so connect one. Press Connect a model in the centre, or open the model row at the foot of the rail. There are three routes. Your own key. Paste a key from Anthropic, Fireworks AI, OpenRouter, Together AI, Groq or DeepInfra. Your messages go straight to that provider, and we charge nothing. Credits. Daimond runs the model for you and draws on a prepaid balance, so there is no provider account to manage. While testing is closed, accounts with credits are given out by passcode. A model of your own. Wählen Sie Custom and give the address of any service that speaks the same chat API, including one running on your own machine. Modelle & Anbieter has the detail."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s4","t":"Say hello","u":"Hier anfangen › Three steps to a first answer","b":"Press Say hello , or the + neben Chats , then type in the box and send. The answer arrives in the centre panel, where you will spend most of your time. The chat takes its title from your first line, so a rail of chats reads as a list of subjects."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s5","t":"Then keep what works","u":"Hier anfangen","b":"A chat is only a conversation. When one has worked something out, press Keep on its row in the rail and it becomes a diamond . A diamond is a saved project with its own memory, page and files. Work inside it starts from what it already knows, so you stop re-explaining yourself. Chats & Diamonds covers it."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s6","t":"What this does that a chat window does not","u":"Hier anfangen","b":"It remembers per subject. A diamond carries what you worked out into every later turn, and you can read and edit that memory as a file. It works on real files. Point it at a folder and it edits the files in place, inside a fence you set. It shows the bill. Each turn is priced on this device as it is spent, from the provider's own figure. It can be checked. The code in this browser is public, builds byte for byte from source, and is sealed into a published record. Verify this build in the About dialog checks the one you are running."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s7","t":"The four words this guide uses","u":"Hier anfangen","b":"diamond , a saved project with its own memory and page. daimon , the assistant that works inside a diamond. crystal , what a diamond knows, kept as a file you can read and edit. forge , the shared board where proposals about Daimond itself are filed, shown in the Improve panel."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s8","t":"What is on screen","u":"Hier anfangen","b":"Der Bildschirm hat drei Zonen. Die Leiste on the left lists your diamonds and chats, and under a movable divider shows your account, one status line and what you have spent. The centre holds the conversation, with whatever you are reading beside it. The Dock on the right holds what you pull from, such as files, mail, running agents and spending. Across the top, each panel has a chip that opens or closes it. A fresh account shows six, for diamonds, Chat, Web, Workspace, Tools and Spending, and the rest are one press away in the gallery behind the ⋯ chip. At the far right are the update chip, About, Link another device , this guide and Settings . Die Oberfläche walks through all of it, and none of it is needed to get an answer."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s9","t":"One status line","u":"Hier anfangen","b":"The foot of the rail. One line says where things stand, and Details opens the rest. Above the spend row is one line, which reads Locked , Not signed in , No model connected , Offline , Synced , oder This device only . It answers the question most worth asking at that moment, showing the most blocking state first. Press it to open Details , which covers models, tools, permissions, storage, machine, sync and the build you are on. Those are diagnostics, so they stay behind the line until you want them."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s10","t":"Griffbereit halten","u":"Hier anfangen","b":"Use your browser's own Installieren , oder Zum Startbildschirm hinzufügen on a phone, and Daimond gets an icon and a window of its own. It is the same page and the same stored work, so nothing is copied and nothing moves. Daimond updates itself, taking a new build at a quiet moment and not in the middle of a running turn or a half-typed message. The chip beside the top-bar buttons says when one is ready."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s11","t":"Where to go next","u":"Hier anfangen","b":""},{"p":"index.html","a":"s12","t":"Chats & Diamonds","u":"Hier anfangen › Where to go next","b":"Reading a long thread, keeping a chat, and what a diamond remembers."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s13","t":"Dateien, E-Mail & das Web","u":"Hier anfangen › Where to go next","b":"Getting files in, sharing a folder to your other devices, mail, and reading a page."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s14","t":"Dein Rechner","u":"Hier anfangen › Where to go next","b":"Letting a daimon edit real folders and run real commands, inside a fence."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s15","t":"Helfer & wo Züge laufen","u":"Hier anfangen › Where to go next","b":"Agents dispatched to work in parallel, and naming the machine that picks turns up."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s16","t":"Sicherheit & Problembehebung","u":"Hier anfangen › Where to go next","b":"What Daimond asks before it acts, what stays private, and what to do when something is wrong."},{"p":"index.html","a":"s17","t":"Ask Daimond","u":"Hier anfangen › Where to go next","b":"The rail holds a diamond called Daimond Help . It answers from this build and from this guide, and says which page an answer came from. Weiter: Die Oberfläche &rarr;"},{"p":"interface.html","a":"","t":"Die Oberfläche","u":"","b":"Die Oberfläche Three zones and a top bar. Once you know the zones, every part of Daimond has a place."},{"p":"interface.html","a":"s1","t":"The rail, on the left","u":"Die Oberfläche","b":"The rail lists what you are working on, with diamonds at the top and Chats under them, newest first. The + on each head makes a new one, and dragging the divider gives one list more room. Above them is the Alles row, a play, a pause and a round light for the whole app. Pause there and nothing runs anywhere until you release it. Below the divider is your account, showing the name you gave, one status line, and what you have spent today, this week and this month. Hier anfangen covers the status line, and Details opens the diagnostics behind it. One of those details is the build you are on. Press it for the release history, which shows what is planned, the build you are running, and every earlier build with its date and its place in a sealed record. You cannot go back to an older build, by design, because an old client holds faults since fixed and may read newer data wrongly."},{"p":"interface.html","a":"s2","t":"The centre","u":"Die Oberfläche","b":"The centre holds the conversation and whatever you are reading beside it. Panels here sit side by side and not over the chat, so you need not leave the conversation to look at something. Width decides how many fit, from two at the narrowest to four at the widest, with one more for roughly every 380 pixels. Narrow the window and the panel opened most recently closes, and the chat is never the one to go. AI holds the conversation, and comes back whenever the centre would otherwise be empty. Web shows a web page, or drives one. Dok shows a file as its characters, with room to read and edit it. Preview shows what a file looks like, whether a picture, a PDF, or typeset pages beside their source. Email message opens one message beside the chat. Werkzeuge lists what Daimond can do. Verfassen is for writing mail, and only you can press Send. Graph draws your diamonds and the links between them. Terminal is a real terminal on your machine. See Dein Rechner ."},{"p":"interface.html","a":"s3","t":"The dock, on the right","u":"Die Oberfläche","b":"The dock holds what you pull from. E-Mail holds your mailboxes. Workspace shows your files as a tree. Agenten lists the helpers running now, with what each is costing. It stays out of the way until the first one runs. Ausgaben shows where the money went. Ausstehend lists what is waiting on you. Each row is answered with Ausführen , discussed, or dropped. Papierkorb holds deleted chats and diamonds for thirty days. Soziales und Improve are covered in Soziales & Vorschläge ."},{"p":"interface.html","a":"s4","t":"Die obere Leiste","u":"Die Oberfläche","b":"The top bar carries the wordmark, a row of chips, and five buttons at the far right, which are the update chip, About, Link another device , this guide, and Settings . Every panel has a chip. Click one to open or close that panel. An open panel's chip is filled in, so the row reads as a map of what is on screen. Chips are grouped by zone in the order the zones sit, and each keeps its position so you can learn it. A fresh account gets six chips, for diamonds, Chat, Web, Workspace, Tools and Spending. The rest live behind the ⋯ chip at the end of the row. Click it for the gallery, which lists every panel there is, searchable and grouped by zone, with a pin on each row that puts it in the bar. A dock chip is greyed when the dock is full, and its tooltip names the fix. Strg K opens any panel or setting by typing."},{"p":"interface.html","a":"s5","t":"Settings","u":"Die Oberfläche","b":"Settings is the last button on the right. It holds how Daimond looks and where things sit, and nothing about what it does. View. Einfach shows names only, and Max puts the model, the cost and the context on every tile. A tile's own cog overrides it. Theme. Eleven palettes in three bands. This guide wears whichever the app is wearing. Text size. Four steps. Only the type changes, so for a bigger interface use the browser's zoom. Side panels. How the dock tiles, and so how many panels it holds, whether four in one column, four at 2&times;2, or six at 2&times;3 or 3&times;2. Auto lets the window decide. Sprache und Currency. Billing is in US dollars whatever the figures show. With a diamond open, the menu also offers to keep the current arrangement of panels with it, and opening that diamond again puts the panels back. It is saved only when you ask."},{"p":"interface.html","a":"s6","t":"The Graph","u":"Die Oberfläche","b":"Open Graph to see your diamonds drawn, with the links between them. Bring the pointer near a tile's edge and four anchors appear. Drag from one and a line follows, snaps to the nearest diamond, and makes the link when you let go. A link can exist with no relation on it, which means only that the two are joined. Chips offer a Relation on the line that has just appeared, and Esc leaves it blank. Let go over empty canvas and a box asks for a name, then a new diamond is made there, already linked. Nothing is written until you give the name. Click a link to select it and press Delete to drop it. Its form carries Reverse , which writes a new record, so the note travels and the date does not. Organise lays everything out again to reduce crossings. From the keyboard, select a diamond, press L , and click the target."},{"p":"interface.html","a":"s7","t":"Mit der Tastatur, und mit dem Ohr","u":"Die Oberfläche","b":"Tab moves through the controls, Enter oder Leertaste operates one, and Esc closes what is open. Every dialog, menu and sheet also carries a cross, sized for a thumb. A dialog keeps focus inside itself and hands it back on closing. With a screen reader, an answer is announced once when it arrives instead of being recited as it is written. The window has named regions and real headings throughout. Anything you cannot reach or cannot hear is a fault, so say so on Soziales ."},{"p":"interface.html","a":"s8","t":"On a phone","u":"Die Oberfläche","b":"Below the phone width the chips give way to the phone shell. The chat is the floor, and a panel rises over it as a sheet you can drag down again. The rail becomes a drawer, opened at the top left, with your account at the foot of it. The row along the bottom is the same chip row, scrolled sideways, and it carries every panel instead of six. The filled chip is what you are looking at, because on a phone only one thing is, so a chip takes you there instead of toggling. Where a row of controls runs off the edge, it scrolls, and fades at the edge to say so. A diamond's page has a full-screen button that gives the whole display to the page. Installed to the home screen, Daimond runs in its own window with no browser furniture and holds clear of the notch. It is the same page and the same stored work. &larr; Start here Next: Chats & diamonds &rarr;"},{"p":"models.html","a":"","t":"Modelle & Anbieter","u":"","b":"Modelle & Anbieter A daimon thinks with a model. Bring a key you already hold and pay that provider directly, or buy credits and let Daimond run one for you."},{"p":"models.html","a":"s1","t":"Your own key","u":"Modelle & Anbieter","b":"Open the model row at the foot of the rail. It lists a key for each provider you use and which model new work starts on. + Anbieter hinzufügen asks the same three questions whoever the provider is. Choose the provider, paste the key, star a default model, then save."},{"p":"models.html","a":"s2","t":"Einen Anbieter wählen","u":"Modelle & Anbieter › Your own key","b":"Anthropic, Fireworks AI, OpenRouter, Together AI, Groq or DeepInfra. Eigener Anbieter reveals a Basis-URL box for any other service speaking the same chat API, including one on your own machine."},{"p":"models.html","a":"s3","t":"Paste the key","u":"Modelle & Anbieter › Your own key","b":"It is stored wrapped under your passphrase, and sent to the provider you chose and to nobody else. It reaches your other devices only inside the encrypted sync parcel, still wrapped."},{"p":"models.html","a":"s4","t":"Ein Standardmodell mit einem Stern markieren","u":"Modelle & Anbieter › Your own key","b":"List models fetches the catalogue where the provider offers one, and otherwise you type the model id. The starred one is where new chats and diamonds begin. Your messages then go straight to that provider on your own account. Daimond is out of the path, and we charge nothing."},{"p":"models.html","a":"s5","t":"Choosing a different model","u":"Modelle & Anbieter","b":"The default is a starting point. Any connected model can be chosen for one chat from the selector in its header, and the default is untouched. A diamond can also carry a separate Helper model for the agents it dispatches, which applies to the next one dispatched and to none already running. Where a model publishes no context window, the tile says Context size unknown for this model. and guesses nothing."},{"p":"models.html","a":"s6","t":"Choosing who serves it","u":"Modelle & Anbieter","b":"A router hands one model to whichever upstream provider it likes, and they are not equally good. Under an OpenRouter provider, each model row carries a Providers field, with the placeholder prefer, -avoid, ! . A bare name prefers that provider. A leading - avoids one. A bare ! means only these, refusing every fallback. So Novita, -DeepInfra prefers one and avoids another. The field is saved as you leave it. A provider whose catalogue has not been fetched keeps its rows behind a Models&hellip; disclosure, so a preference already set stays reachable."},{"p":"models.html","a":"s7","t":"Guthaben","u":"Modelle & Anbieter","b":"Credits run the model for you with no key needed, and they also meter the few things that leave the browser: fetching a page, the bandwidth of mail and of cross-device sync, and cloud storage beyond the free tier. Sync, Email and cloud storage themselves are turned on by Daimond Pro, and metered use is paid from credits with or without it. Open the credits row for your balance and the packs. Credits are not a subscription, and you keep what you buy. Payment happens on the payment provider's own hosted page, so no card number is typed into Daimond. While testing is closed, new accounts with credits are given out by passcode. Daimond works with your own provider key without one."},{"p":"models.html","a":"s8","t":"Automatische Aufladung","u":"Modelle & Anbieter","b":"Auto-reload is a standing instruction to buy credits when they run low, so a long job does not stop halfway. It is the one place Daimond may charge a saved card while you are away, so it is deliberately explicit. Three numbers set it. Mindestsaldo is the balance at which a top-up fires. So viel kaufen is how much one top-up adds. Never spend more, per month, than is a hard cap on the calendar month. Set this one carefully. It is enforced on the same code path as the charge. It cannot be switched on without a saved card, because a control that turned on and then failed silently would be worse than one that is disabled and says why. &larr; Social & proposals Next: Spending &rarr;"},{"p":"social.html","a":"","t":"Soziales & Vorschläge","u":"","b":"Soziales & Vorschläge Two panels and one diamond. Soziales is where you tell us something. Improve is the board it arrives on. Pending is where anything waiting on you turns up."},{"p":"social.html","a":"s1","t":"Saying something","u":"Soziales & Vorschläge","b":"Offen Soziales and write. The first line is the title, and what happened goes under it. Senden sends what is on screen and the build id, and nothing else goes with it. Posting needs a posting name , which the app calls your voice. Without one you can read everything and keep a note to this device. The panel says so in one row, Set a posting name to send. , mit Get one beside it. It takes one tap, and it is part of Daimond Pro."},{"p":"social.html","a":"s2","t":"A note that can be acted on","u":"Soziales & Vorschläge › Saying something","b":"A note needs three things, in this order. Leave any of them out and the note needs a conversation before anything can be done. Where it is. Which panel, and which part of it. What you expected. What happened instead. The build id is attached for you, so you need not find it."},{"p":"social.html","a":"s3","t":"Naming where","u":"Soziales & Vorschläge › Saying something","b":"There are four regions, and they are the ones this guide uses throughout: the obere Leiste , the Leiste links, die centre , and the Dock on the right. On a phone, the drawer is the rail and a sheet is a dock panel. Inside a region, these are the words worth knowing. Chip , the small pill in the top bar. Kachel , a diamond, a chat or an agent in a list. Kopf , a section's heading row. Zahnrad , the settings for the thing it sits on. Licht , the round one beside a play and a pause. Verfasser , the message box and its buttons. Zeile und Dialog , which mean what they say. \"The cog on the Life log tile\" is unambiguous, and \"the settings button\" is not."},{"p":"social.html","a":"s4","t":"The board","u":"Soziales & Vorschläge","b":"Improve shows what has been proposed and what is being done about it, in four columns: Awaiting you , Greenlit (accepted, not built yet), Shipped , and Dropped . Reading needs nothing. Voting and commenting need a posting name. Only we can add or move a card, and the board says nothing about who decides. If it cannot be reached it says Could not load. and nothing more, because that is all it knows."},{"p":"social.html","a":"s5","t":"Pending","u":"Soziales & Vorschläge","b":"Pending , in the dock, holds what is waiting on you, which is a daimon asking permission for something, and proposals about your own account. Sort by priority, newest or oldest. Each row is answered one of three ways, Do it , Discuss it first , oder Drop it . Empty, it says Nothing waiting on you."},{"p":"social.html","a":"s6","t":"The Optimiser","u":"Soziales & Vorschläge","b":"Your rail holds a diamond called Daimond Optimiser . It finds what should have been written down, what should have been cheaper and what should have been automatic, and hands you the change to make. It reads counts kept on this device, meaning turns, spend, models and tool calls, and nothing else. It does not see what any conversation was about. It ships stopped, and only you can start it. Open its settings with the cog on its tile, find the action After 30 minutes of your activity , and press play on the light beside it. After that it reads the counts every half hour you actually work. What it finds arrives as a tile in Pending , wherever you happen to be, with a headline, the evidence under it, and Do it . The note on the tile says where it came from, Found by its diamond. &ldquo;Do it&rdquo; asks that diamond to carry it out. Nothing is held open by one, so the tick is a fresh instruction, not a permission you gave earlier. The Optimiser alone is denied two things, because it runs while nobody is looking. It cannot publish in your name, and it cannot dispatch helpers."},{"p":"social.html","a":"s7","t":"People, messages and sharing","u":"Soziales & Vorschläge","b":"Personen connects you to somebody directly. Show your code to them in the room, or read theirs. From there you have private messages between the two of you, and groups. A group can be closed by whoever made it, and then nothing already said is taken away and nothing new arrives. A diamond can be shared with somebody you are connected to. The shared diamond carries its memory and its page, and both are sealed to the people you sent it to. Each of these depends on the relay being switched on. Where it is not, the panel says so in one line, and offers no control that would fail. &larr; More than one device Next: Models & providers &rarr;"},{"p":"spending.html","a":"","t":"Ausgaben","u":"","b":"Ausgaben Model calls are priced on this device, as they happen, from the provider's own figure. The bill arrives in front of you as it is spent, wherever the provider reports a figure, and not later as a surprise."},{"p":"spending.html","a":"s1","t":"Zwei Töpfe, getrennt gehalten","u":"Ausgaben","b":"The two pots are different accounts in different currencies, so they are shown as two tracks and not added together. Inference covers the model calls billed to your key . They are recorded here per turn, and none of them passes through us. Guthaben holds the prepaid balance, spent on the model when Daimond runs it for you and on what leaves the browser, web, mail, sync , and cloud storage. The foot of the rail carries the running figures for today, this week and this month. Press one to open the Ausgaben panel, which shows a headline figure per pot, a daily graph, a breakdown by category, and a plain table of movements."},{"p":"spending.html","a":"s2","t":"What stops a runaway","u":"Ausgaben","b":"A workspace that runs many agents at once can spend quickly, and the danger lies in a sudden rate more than in a large monthly total. Four measures catch the rate, and none asks you to set a limit in advance. A pace check before a fan-out. The cost of dispatching a batch is known before any of it starts. A batch that would run faster than your own recent pace is held, and Daimond asks once, with the number on the prompt. A few helpers of ordinary cost do not trip it, and a sudden fifty do. Anhalten und Stoppen, immer griffbereit. Die Agenten panel pauses everything running, or stops it. The Alles row at the top of the rail pauses the whole app. A paused thing refuses a turn before it starts, so a look costs nothing. Ein eigener Schlüssel für jeden Agenten. Each helper running on credits spends its own freshly minted key, capped against what is left after its siblings' claims. No two share a key, so parallel helpers cannot race one allowance past its cap. Alles gemessen, Zug um Zug, auf Ihrem Gerät. Every call is priced and recorded as it happens, and the graphs are drawn from that record."},{"p":"spending.html","a":"s3","t":"A ceiling you set","u":"Ausgaben","b":"Settings carries a per-turn spend cap. A turn that reaches the round limit continues on its own, so this cap is the ceiling that holds a runaway. It applies where the provider reports what a round cost, and only there."},{"p":"spending.html","a":"s4","t":"Watching one agent","u":"Ausgaben","b":"Each tile in Agenten shows its cost as it accrues, in tokens and in money, and not only at the end. Under the header a line says how many are running, paused and queued, which makes the size of a fan-out legible before you decide whether to hold it. The aim is a team of agents you can run without fear that a loop, or a fan-out larger than you realised, can cost more than a glance and a click can undo. &larr; Models & providers Next: Safety & fixes &rarr;"},{"p":"sync.html","a":"","t":"Mehr als ein Gerät","u":"","b":"Mehr als ein Gerät Daimond keeps your work on the device you are using, so a second device starts empty. Link it, and your chats, diamonds and files stay in step without the server ever reading them. What crosses is one encrypted parcel, and only your devices hold the key to it. The key comes from your passphrase and does not leave the browser."},{"p":"sync.html","a":"s1","t":"Link a second device","u":"Mehr als ein Gerät","b":"Each device makes its own identity, so typing your passphrase into a fresh browser starts a eigenes account. To use the one you have, link the new device to it."},{"p":"sync.html","a":"s2","t":"Auf dem Gerät, das Sie schon nutzen, den Verknüpfungsdialog öffnen","u":"Mehr als ein Gerät › Link a second device","b":"Weiteres Gerät verknüpfen in the top bar shows a QR code and a one-time pairing code. Ihr erstes Gerät zeigt einen QR-Code und einen Code."},{"p":"sync.html","a":"s3","t":"On the new device, scan the QR or type the code","u":"Mehr als ein Gerät › Link a second device","b":"Point the phone's camera at the code. It opens Daimond and fills the code in, so you only tap Dieses Gerät verknüpfen . Without a camera, open Daimond there, choose Have a passcode or a pairing code? , and type it. After scanning, one tap."},{"p":"sync.html","a":"s4","t":"Mit derselben Passphrase entsperren","u":"Mehr als ein Gerät › Link a second device","b":"The new device now holds your account. Use the passphrase you already have, and your work appears. A passkey can unlock it faster afterwards. If a device asks you to create a passphrase instead of entering one, it is about to start a new account. Go back and pair it, or import a backup. One account, one passphrase, on every device you link. The passphrase cannot travel on its own, because it only decrypts a key the device already holds, so a browser that has never been linked has nothing for it to open."},{"p":"sync.html","a":"s5","t":"Was mitreist","u":"Mehr als ein Gerät","b":"Your chats, your diamonds and the way you laid them out, your mail, your workspace files, the devices on the account, and what you have paused all travel. Any kind of file travels, up to a gigabyte each. So does the Trash, so a deletion and a restore both reach every device. What syncs is also what is kept in cloud storage, so a workspace can be larger than the device reading it. A file that is not here still shows in the tree and comes down when asked for. A folder you opened on one computer is not in the browser's storage, so it does not travel by default. Dateien, E-Mail & das Web covers the per-folder control that copies one to devices that cannot open it."},{"p":"sync.html","a":"s6","t":"Running a turn somewhere else","u":"Mehr als ein Gerät","b":"When more than one of your devices is awake, one can run a turn for another and the answer syncs back. One switch turns it on, Hand off when you step away . A turn on this computer then moves to another awake device when you close it, whether the lid shuts, the tab closes or the connection drops, and finishes there. Helfer & wo Züge laufen covers naming the machine that should pick turns up, and the two things that stop it. An errand sent to another device, and the answer it sends back, are sealed to your account like everything else. The server routes a parcel it cannot open."},{"p":"sync.html","a":"s7","t":"Was es kostet","u":"Mehr als ein Gerät","b":"Die geräteübergreifende Synchronisierung gehört zu Daimond Pro , at $8 a month, billed monthly, and you can cancel any time. Pro also turns on cloud storage, Email and a posting name. Away for a month, the billing pauses on its own and resumes when you are back. Without Pro a device works on its own and loses nothing. Inference, bandwidth and other metered use are paid from credits either way. &larr; Helpers & where turns run Next: Social & proposals &rarr;"}],"alias":null};
